# Docker build context for infra/Dockerfile.{api,worker,web}.
#
# The context is the repository root so the pnpm workspace manifests and the
# package sources are available. Keep this list aggressive: anything matched here
# never leaves the host, so it can never be baked into an image or slow a build.

# --- secrets / local environment -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.tapeci
infra/env.prod
infra/*.env.prod
*.pem
*.key

# --- dependencies / caches --------------------------------------------------
# These are large local caches (several GB in a working checkout). They are
# re-created inside the image by `pnpm install`; shipping them only inflates the
# build context and can leak host state into the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.pnpm-cache
.npm-cache
.corepack
**/.turbo
**/coverage

# --- build output -----------------------------------------------------------
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- tests / fixtures / evidence -------------------------------------------
tests
**/test-results
**/test-results-live
**/playwright-report
apps/web/e2e
apps/web/e2e-live
docs/evidence

# --- VCS / editor / OS ------------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
superpowers
.superpowers
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# --- docs / misc ------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
artifacts
logs
TapeCI_PRD_Technical_Design.md
